From 4127b473b6b66593efdf5b8ca53a6ec0cc77267a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 14:41:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] updates: the verified file of the channel is the only update
 left, read back before it is kept

A review of the update channel of LibreELEC Hades found three gaps between
what the client checks and what the next start installs:

- the init installs the first .tar of /storage/.update by name (or an
  image, or KERNEL and SYSTEM), and the client did not look at what else
  was there: another .tar named before the file of the channel (one put
  there by hand, through the share Update or by anything that runs as
  root) was installed in its place, and the verified file deleted. Now,
  before the file of the channel is kept, and again when one downloaded
  before waits for the next start, every other update in that folder is
  removed and named in the log (a warning); one that cannot be removed (a
  folder) stops the download, and nothing is kept;
- the SHA-256 was computed on the bytes as they came, not on the file that
  was kept: something that wrote into the part file meanwhile changed what
  was installed, and the download still said that it held. The file is now
  read back through the same descriptor after it is written and flushed,
  and kept only when its size and SHA-256 are the signed ones, and only
  when the name moved into the update folder is still that file;
- a channel whose manifest is gone after one was taken from it (by mistake
  in a release, or taken away) said "nothing newer" as information. The
  log now says it as a warning: a newer version, if there is one, cannot
  be told. A channel that never had one stays as it was.
